BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 671.55 Tm (Bruce Hill and colleague David run opposite sequences on the same probate list. David mails first. Bruce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 656.32 Tm (calls first and does the math out loud. On 100 leads, roughly 50% answer in month one, which buys 50) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 641.10 Tm (conversations for about $400 of ISA cost. A six-month campaign of 600 mailers at $1.50 apiece costs $900) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 625.87 Tm (and pulls inbound calls from about 5% [y1TInRM-Flc @ 00:00:43]. Bruce concedes that mail responders) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 610.65 Tm (arrive hot while the phone conversations do not, but turns about 25 of the 50 into marketable pipeline: 'I do it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 595.42 Tm (my way because I get a bigger pipeline.' An All The Leads subscriber wanted to mail first so the opener) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 580.20 Tm (could be 'did you receive my letter.' Bruce called that semi-valid but mostly an excuse to put off calling, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 564.97 Tm (told the asker to practice and build better scripts [omZ157LG-W8 @ 00:03:57]. Rick of More Flip with Rick) Tj ET
